# renders/ holds BOTH generated output and source. Under renders/yaris_render_s1/
# alone there are 24 top-level .py source files against 881 non-.py files at any
# depth. (Corrected 2026-08-12: an earlier version of this comment, and the message
# of commit 00b735c, said "501 generated artifacts". That 501 was a -maxdepth 2
# count restricted to four extensions, not a total, and it is wrong as stated. The
# commit message cannot be corrected without rewriting history, so it stands wrong;
# this comment is the correction.) A blanket
# "renders/" ignored the source too, which meant sim_standing.py, vehicle_live.py
# and gates*.py had NO commit history at all, even though the corrections
# register cites them by file:line as the primary source for the
# canonical facts (A1, A2, A5, F5) and even though solidify_watertight /
# is_gaussian_ply, named as Contribution #1, is implemented there. An authorship
# claim over an untracked working file cannot be dated or evidenced.
# Git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded, so the blanket
# "renders/" is replaced by a walk-down: ignore the contents at each level, then
# re-include the next directory, then finally re-include only *.py.
# Corrected 2026-08-12. Generated output stays ignored.
renders/*
!renders/yaris_render_s1/
renders/yaris_render_s1/*
!renders/yaris_render_s1/*.py
!data/track1_sweep_v1/
!data/track1_sweep_v1/**
!data/track1_sweep_v2/
!data/track1_sweep_v2/**
# data/* above silently hides the canonical 17-run results stores. They were only ever
# tracked by force-add (841d666), so a new sibling file lands invisible unless un-ignored
# here. Register D6a. Keep this list in step with analysis/classify_failure_modes.py.
!data/all_runs_inventory.csv
# Non-canonical floor-friction and three-vehicle study, cited by the paper (Section IV-C).
!data/three_class_*_2026-08-14.csv
!data/failure_modes_by_run.json
!data/failure_modes_by_run_classified.csv
vehicle_geometry_research/**/*.key
vehicle_geometry_research/**/*-detailed-*/**/*.key

vehicle_meshes/
*.key
_PENDING_NOT_COMMITTED/
can-it-ford/
_ARCHIVE_*
.olauth
deliverables/
*.rtfd/
out/
overleaf_sync/
figures/_BIG/
figures/_BIG_PREVIEW/

# Overleaf-canonical working copy. paper/ is not edited in this repo
# (the paper builds from conference_101719_1.tex on the overleaf remote, not from
# here), so this local snapshot must never enter history and diverge from it.
paper/canonical_2026-08-02/

